## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Phase 2 — Disk space:** FAERS full corpus (2004–2024) requires ~25GB. Is this feasible, or should we scope to last 4 quarters (~3GB) for the initial implementation?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Phase 4 — Kafka:** Kafka adds Docker dependency (already used for HBase). Should the pipeline section be Kafka-real OR pivoted to a simpler `asyncio` queue + background worker if Docker is unavailable? Kafka gives a better portfolio story but is heavier.

> [!NOTE]
> **GNNExplainer vs SHAP for GNN:** PyTorch Geometric's `GNNExplainer` gives edge/node masks natively. SHAP `DeepExplainer` works on the GNN if we treat it as a black-box. GNNExplainer is more interpretable for graphs; SHAP is easier to visualize in the existing UI. Recommend GNNExplainer for the portfolio narrative.

> [!NOTE]
> **Phase 3 — Bradford Hill UI:** The 9-criteria assessment could be a modal form OR a dedicated tab. Given the Signals tab is already dense, recommend a slide-over drawer panel.

